  user_input {
    user_response: "MUST Haves (High Impact for a Snippet Tool)\nFully Offline App Shell (Precaching): Since you have a Service Worker, we must cache the app assets (HTML, CSS, JS) on initial load, not just fallback. This ensures the app loads instantly even on a subway with no cell service.\nWeb Share Target API: Since it\'s a PWA, we can register it as a \"Share Target\". This means a user can highlight text in any other app (like a browser or email client), tap \"Share\", and select \"QuickReply\" to instantly save it as a new snippet.\nKeyboard Shortcuts: Add a Cmd+K (or Ctrl+K) listener to instantly snap focus to the search bar. Speed is everything for this tool.\n\342\234\250 SHOULD Haves (Quality of Life)\nVariables / Placeholders: Support snippets like \"Hi {Name}, your order is shipped!\". When they tap \"Copy,\" a tiny modal asks for the {Name} and then copies the final string.\n\"Most Used\" Sorting: Track a small counter every time a user taps \"Copy\" on a snippet, and add an option to sort by \"Most frequently used\" rather than just categories.\n\n\nWhich of these you suggest implimenting"
    items {
      text: "MUST Haves (High Impact for a Snippet Tool)\nFully Offline App Shell (Precaching): Since you have a Service Worker, we must cache the app assets (HTML, CSS, JS) on initial load, not just fallback. This ensures the app loads instantly even on a subway with no cell service.\nWeb Share Target API: Since it\'s a PWA, we can register it as a \"Share Target\". This means a user can highlight text in any other app (like a browser or email client), tap \"Share\", and select \"QuickReply\" to instantly save it as a new snippet.\nKeyboard Shortcuts: Add a Cmd+K (or Ctrl+K) listener to instantly snap focus to the search bar. Speed is everything for this tool.\n\342\234\250 SHOULD Haves (Quality of Life)\nVariables / Placeholders: Support snippets like \"Hi {Name}, your order is shipped!\". When they tap \"Copy,\" a tiny modal asks for the {Name} and then copies the final string.\n\"Most Used\" Sorting: Track a small counter every time a user taps \"Copy\" on a snippet, and add an option to sort by \"Most frequently used\" rather than just categories.\n\n\nWhich of these you suggest implimenting"
