    modified_response: "I highly recommend implementing **all of these features**, as they perfectly align with building a fast, mobile-first productivity tool. Here is a brief look at why they are excellent additions:\n\n**The MUST Haves (Speed & Reliability)**\n*   **Fully Offline App Shell**: Essential for a true PWA experience. We can update your existing Service Worker (`sw.js`) to cache the HTML, CSS, and JS shell on the first load so it opens instantly anywhere, regardless of signal strength.\n*   **Web Share Target API**: This is a killer feature for a snippet manager. We can configure `manifest.ts` so that when a user highlights text in another app (like Chrome or Gmail) and taps \"Share\", they can push it straight into QuickReply as a new snippet.\n*   **Keyboard Shortcuts (Cmd+K)**: Since speed is the primary focus, a quick keyboard listener to instantly focus the search bar is a perfect, low-effort/high-reward addition.\n\n**The SHOULD Haves (Quality of Life)**\n*   **Variables / Placeholders**: Allowing snippets like `\"Hi {Name}...\"` with a micro-prompt upon copying elevates the tool from a simple clipboard manager to a smart workflow automation app.\n*   **\"Most Used\" Sorting**: Tracking usage counts and sorting by frequency ensures the user\'s most critical snippets naturally bubble to the top without manual organization.\n\nWould you like me to go ahead and implement all of these features into the application for you?"
