  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Outlining the Plan**\n\nI\'m now putting together the plan requested. My first step is focusing on the \"must-haves.\" Right now, I\'m diving into creating a fully offline app shell. I\'ll modify `public/sw.js` for precaching strategies, looking at `install` and `activate` to cache HTML, CSS, and JS components.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Here is the plan for implementing the **MUST HAVE** and **SHOULD HAVE** features:\n\n### 1. Fully Offline App Shell (Precaching)\n**Approach**: I will update the existing `public/sw.js` (Service Worker) to include an `install` event that aggressively precaches the core application UI (HTML, Next.js JS bundles, and CSS chunks). I\342\200\231ll implement a Cache-First strategy (with network fallback) for static assets, and a Network-First strategy (with cache fallback) for any initial page loads, guaranteeing a fast offline experience.\n\n### 2. Web Share Target API\n**Approach**: \n- Modify `app/manifest.ts` to add a `share_target` configuration set up to receive incoming text shares.\n- The `share_target` will redirect shared text to a specific path or URL parameter (e.g., `/?shared_text=...`).\n- Add a `useEffect` hook in `app/page.tsx` to detect this parameter on load. When present, it will automatically open the \"New Snippet\" bottom sheet with the shared text pre-filled so the user can quickly categorize and save it.\n\n### 3. Keyboard Shortcuts (Cmd+K / Ctrl+K)\n**Approach**: \n- Create a `useRef` for the Search input field in `app/page.tsx`.\n- Attach a global `keydown` event listener in a `useEffect`.\n- When the `Cmd+K` or `Ctrl+K` key combination is pressed, intercept the event (`e.preventDefault()`) and call `.focus()` on the search ref to immediately let the user start typing.\n\n### 4. Variables / Placeholders Support\n**Approach**:\n- Create a visual parser inside the snippet card that highlights text spanning `{}` like `{Name}` or `{Order ID}`.\n- When the user taps the **Copy** button on a snippet containing placeholders, I will intercept the copy action.\n- A small popup/modal will appear prompting the user for exactly those required variables. \n- Upon confirming, the script interpolates the variables into the string and copies the final version to the clipboard.\n\n### 5. \"Most Used\" Sorting\n**Approach**: \n- Update the `Snippet` type to include a `useCount` number (defaulting to `0`).\n- Update the `handleCopyText` function to increment this counter each time a snippet is copied and persist it to localStorage.\n- Add a tiny \"Sort\" toggle near the categories (Sort by: Latest | Most Used). Modify the `filteredSnippets` memo function to reorder snippets based on the `useCount` variable if the user has that filter selected.\n\nWould you like me to begin implementing this plan for you?"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 2
      nanos: 36111016
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
