  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Offline Capability**\n\nI\'m focusing on the offline app shell. The plan is to modify the `/public/sw.js` file to precache the essential assets during the `install` event. This includes the HTML for the root (`/`), and the core CSS/JS. Next.js integration should streamline the process.\n\n\n**Caching Core Assets**\n\nI\'ve got caching the essential assets dialed in now! I\'m caching the root, service worker, and manifest files. I\'m leveraging a generic strategy to cache all other requests using `stale-while-revalidate` or `cache-first`. This should make the site quite resilient in offline scenarios.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "Here is the plan for how I will approach adding these features:\n\n### 1. Fully Offline App Shell (Precaching)\n**Approach:** I will update the `/public/sw.js` file to use a stronger offline-first caching strategy. Instead of relying solely on network-first (which is slow when the connection is spotty), I will implement caching for the core endpoints (like `/`) during the install phase. I\'ll also add a combination of `Cache-First` for static assets and `Stale-While-Revalidate` for navigation requests to ensure immediate loading on repeated visits, even without cell service.\n\n### 2. Web Share Target API\n**Approach:** \n- I will modify `/app/manifest.ts` to register the PWA as a `share_target`. This tells the operating system that `QuickReply` can receive shared text.\n- I\'ll add logic to `/app/page.tsx` that reads incoming query parameters (e.g., `?title=...&text=...`). When QuickReply is opened via a share action, I\'ll automatically strip out the shared text, pop open the \"New Snippet\" bottom-sheet, and pre-fill the text area so the user can just select a category and hit \"Save\".\n\n### 3. Keyboard Shortcuts (Cmd/Ctrl + K)\n**Approach:** I will add a `useRef` to the search input field in `/app/page.tsx`. Then, I\'ll set up a global `keydown` event listener in a `useEffect` hook. When it detects `Meta+K` or `Ctrl+K`, it will call `e.preventDefault()` (to stop the browser\'s default search) and instantly trigger `.focus()` on the search bar. Quick and frictionless.\n\n### 4. Variables / Placeholders ({Name})\n**Approach:**\n- When the user taps \"Copy\" on a snippet, I will run a Regular Expression (`/\\{([^}]+)\\}/g`) to detect any placeholders in the text.\n- If placeholders exist, copying will temporarily pause. I will open a streamlined \"Fast-Fill Modal\" mapping each extracted variable to an input field.\n- As they type, it will swap out the placeholders in a preview. Hitting Enter or tapping \"Copy Filled\" will execute the final clipboard copy.\n\n### 5. \"Most Used\" Sorting\n**Approach:** \n- I will extend the `Snippet` data structure to include a `usageCount` integer.\n- Inside the \"Copy\" function, I\'ll increment this count and save it to `localStorage`.\n- I\'ll add a minimal, elegant toggle near the category tabs or search bar allowing users to switch the list sorting between \"Recent\" (default) and \"Most Used\" (sorted descending by `usageCount`).\n\nWould you like me to begin implementing this plan?"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 471928083
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
