  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Offline Access**\n\nI\'m currently focused on developing a fully offline app shell. My plan involves modifying `sw.js` to handle an `install` event for precaching critical assets, and a `fetch` event that prioritizes cached resources. I\'m leaning toward implementing `Stale-While-Revalidate` and `CacheFirst` strategies in the `fetch` event to ensure a seamless experience, even with intermittent connectivity.\n\n\n**Refining Asset Caching**\n\nI\'ve decided to cache the primary app shell route (`/`) as a static asset, using the `Network` as a fallback. I\'ll focus on `sw.js`, instead of Workbox, for this implementation. My main focus is on creating a robust `sw.js` file now.\n\n\n**Adding Variable Handling**\n\nI\'m now integrating variable replacement within snippets, triggered by a regex check for curly brace expressions like `{variableName}`. I\'ll utilize a `VariableReplacerModal` state to prompt the user for each variable. Upon copy, I\'ll parse the snippet body for matches, updating `variableSnippet` and `variablesToFill`, and opening a bottom sheet. This handles interactive variable input.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 6
      nanos: 240262005
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
