  planner_response {
    modified_response: "I have successfully implemented the requested MUST and SHOULD HAVE features to make QuickReply faster and fully offline-capable:\n\n- **Fully Offline App Shell**: Updated the Service Worker (`sw.js`) with a robust asset precaching strategy. The homepage now serves Cache-First for static assets and Network-First (with cache fallback) for the application shell, ensuring it will load instantly even with zero network connectivity.\n- **Web Share Target API**: Integrated `share_target` into the `manifest.ts` file, configuring the PWA to accept incoming shared text. Modified the Next.js page initialization to capture URL parameters (`text`, `title`, or `url`), prefilling the inputs allowing users to share text from browsers/emails directly into a new snippet.\n- **Lightning Search Shortcut**: Injected a keyboard shortcut listener so pressing **Cmd+K** or **Ctrl+K** instantly snaps cursor focus to the search bar for friction-less finding.\n- **Variable Placeholders**: Added a dynamic substring replacer. When you tap \"Copy\" on a snippet containing `{VariableName}` format variables, the app now intercepts the copy and slides up a localized bottom sheet prompting you to fill in variables (e.g. `{Name}`) before instantly copying the clean, finalized variation.\n- **\"Most Used\" Sorting Engine**: Expanded the Snippet data model to persist a `useCount` parameter locally. Added a toggle control to the upper right navigation allowing you to instantly re-sort snippets by either \"Recent\" chronological views or \"Most Used\" descending order to optimize recurring use-cases."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
